# Local Data Workbench — example environment configuration
#
# Copy to .env.local for local overrides:
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# .env.local is git-ignored. Nothing here is a secret; the proof of concept
# runs entirely on the local machine and requires no credentials.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend (Next.js)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Loaded automatically by Next.js from .env.local / .env, and read by
# next.config.mjs. None of these is a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable, so none is inlined
# into the browser bundle: the browser addresses the backend only as the
# same-origin path /forge-api/... and never learns FastAPI's address at all
# (build plan Phase 6, architectural rules 7-9).

# Where the Next.js server forwards /forge-api/* requests.
# Unset, it is built from FORGEXL_BACKEND_HOST and FORGEXL_BACKEND_PORT below,
# so a moved backend port only has to be set once. Set this only to point at a
# backend those two variables cannot describe.
# FORGEXL_BACKEND_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# Extra hostnames allowed to load `next dev` assets, comma-separated.
# next.config.mjs already allows the private IPv4 ranges and *.local names a
# second laptop uses on a trusted LAN (build plan 6G.6). Add a host here only
# if you reach the development machine by some other name.
# FORGEXL_DEV_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=my-macbook.lan

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend (FastAPI)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read from the process environment by backend/app/config.py, which holds the
# defaults below. The backend does not read this file, so override these by
# exporting them in the shell that starts the backend, e.g.
#
#     FORGEXL_BACKEND_PORT=8001 npm run dev
#
# Loopback only. Do not bind to 0.0.0.0 — the app is intentionally local-only.
# FORGEXL_BACKEND_HOST=127.0.0.1
# FORGEXL_BACKEND_PORT=8000

# Where Run directories (inputs, working files, exports, manifests) are stored.
# Defaults to <repository root>/data.
# FORGEXL_DATA_DIRECTORY=

# Maximum accepted size of a single uploaded file, in bytes. Default 250 MB.
# FORGEXL_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=262144000

# Comma-separated CORS allowlist. Never use a wildcard.
# FORGEXL_ALLOWED_FRONTEND_ORIGINS=http://127.0.0.1:3000,http://localhost:3000